message: "If you use this repository or its results, please cite the work below."
type: software
title: "Reconstruction-independent moment tests for sample-based spectral functions"
authors:
  - family-names: "Bonilla Vargas"
    given-names: "Nicolás"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6155-4391"
    affiliation: "Universidad Nacional de Colombia, Bogotá, Colombia; SRH University, Munich, Germany; Daita AI, Munich, Germany"
    email: "ngbonillav@unal.edu.co"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nicolasbonilla/reconstruction-independent-moment-tests"
url: "https://github.com/nicolasbonilla/reconstruction-independent-moment-tests"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a necessary-condition test of sample-based spectral functions A(ω). The moments
  of a reconstruction are compared with full-operator moments <J†(H-e0)^k J> evaluated on the same
  subspace ground state; their difference is exactly the probe's leak out of the subspace at order k
  (the missed spectral weight at k=0, zero through order 2K+1 on a subspace that contains the order-K
  Krylov space). The repository holds the exact sector-Lanczos/Haydock engine, the leak-identity and
  estimator-form checks, a pre-registered, hash-sealed blinded calibration in simulation (300 instances,
  oracle estimator: all 56 truncations and 45 of 61 spurious features rejected, 0 of 71 under-converged
  Krylov reconstructions as implemented, at a false-positive rate of 1/112; at the noise scale of the
  sealed text the false-positive rate is 40/112 and noise also rejects 23 Krylov reconstructions, 17 of
  them exact through m2), the exact limits of a pass at orders 0-2 (including full-support Rayleigh-Ritz, which
  passes with relative L1 error 0.93), and the raw counts and reference samplers of an IBM Heron
  (ibm_fez) run in which the device supplies only sampled supports. Every moment is evaluated
  classically. The record of the sealed on-device n_k test (not run; no job submitted) is included.
